{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "sourceParent": "2d702d38d873c648bfa2141830cfd8beb2c9a290",
  "classification": "Shared source and model-output redaction correction; bounded technical qualification, not model/skill or complete issue acceptance",
  "repair": [
    "Use public TypeScript, Java CST and YAML syntax ownership to retain type/declaration metadata while masking private literal values, decoded copies and overlapping configured literals.",
    "Apply the same source projection after existing guarded reads to discovery, search, excerpts, import graphs and persisted index version10. Unknown/unsafe source projection retains existing omission uncertainty.",
    "Keep unsupported private quotes, nested YAML, unfinished code and private-key material private until a completed safe publication boundary. Cancelled or failed generations discard pending private data.",
    "Separate completed standalone PEM intervals from code parsing at identical UTF-16 offsets and CR/LF coordinates; retain lexical-error refusals outside them. Public malformed fragments without a private literal or strict-redaction candidate remain observed; this is not compilation proof.",
    "Split complete safe BFF blocks by actual writable transport headroom without changing buffer or model grants. Preserve UTF-16 surrogate pairs and abort admission.",
    "Put code-redaction revision on existing evidence-details sibling, keeping source-details at its existing48-field cap and all canonical metadata complete."
  ],
